from 题库接口 import op, mc, block, lines

lines(1,'起点诊断：14项独立任务',r'''
The service is free for residents, but visitors must pay. 能否推出“对所有人免费”？|不能。|residents限定居民；visitors must pay直接反证everyone。检查对象与范围，不凭free一个词。
The study that the team published attracted attention. 写主干。|The study attracted attention.（这项研究引起关注）|that the team published修饰study；team不是attracted的主语。
The bridge being repaired now will open in July. 哪个是主句谓语？谁被维修？|will open；bridge被维修。|being repaired now整体修饰bridge，不能把repair读成桥在维修其他东西。
Not all readers agreed. 是否等于No readers agreed？|不是；并非所有人同意，不等于无人同意。|前句否定全体一致，仍可能有一部分人同意。
原文may help reduce waste，选项has eliminated waste，指出差异。|可能帮助减少，变成已经彻底消除。|情态、时间和程度都被强化，不能当同义改写。
对方说Thank you for the directions，回答“I am sorry for being late”是否合适？|通常不合适；可回应You're welcome。|前句表示感谢，不是在讨论迟到；回答语法成立也不代表交际功能对应。
periodic checks可近义改成regular checks还是constant checks？|regular checks。|定期检查不等于不间断检查，程度和时间分布要保留。
一段先说计划的好处，后说维护费用很高，常用however还是therefore连接？|however。|这是好处与代价的对比；省时本身没有被证明是费用高的原因。
原文说部分学习者更喜欢晚间课程，能否推出学校将取消白天课程？|不能。|偏好不等于已作出的取消决定，还额外加入未来政策。
“一页报名表”的例子出现在“小改变能消除障碍”之后，作用是什么？|具体说明小改变怎样消除参与障碍。|作用题回答例子与论点的关系，不只复述表格长短。
评论说“I support the aim, but the fee is unfair”，是否完全反对目标？|不是；支持目标，批评收费方式。|要分清目标和措施，以及but两边的不同评价。
词框flexible／access／reduce，补have ... to materials。|have access to materials。|have access to表示能够使用；flexible是形容词，reduce是动词，不能直接填在这个搭配位置。
翻译：Although it was useful, it was not available to everyone.|虽然它很有用，但并非每个人都能使用它。|让步、有用、可获得性和not everyone的部分否定都要保留。
改正：Online courses useful, they saves time.|Online courses are useful because they save time. 也可拆为两个完整句子。|补are；复数they配save；两个独立分句不能只用逗号连接，需合适连接词或标点。
''')

lines(2,'主干、从句和指代：20个新情境',r'''
The books that the charity collected last winter are stored upstairs. 找主语核心和主句谓语，并翻译。（charity慈善机构；store存放）|books；are stored。慈善机构去年冬天收集的书存放在楼上。|that ... winter修饰books，collected属于从句；主句是被动存放关系。
Researchers who worked with local schools found that smaller classes were not always more effective. 划出两层从句并译出not always。（effective有效的）|who worked with local schools修饰Researchers；that ... effective是found的内容。小班并不总是更有效。|两个从句处在不同层次；not always不等于never。
The proposal that the council rejected would have reduced parking fees. 谁拒绝什么？主句讨论什么？（council委员会；reject拒绝）|委员会拒绝了提案；主句说该提案本可以降低停车费。|council是rejected的主语，proposal是其对象；would have reduced带未实现的过去可能，不能说费用已经降低。
The fact that many users returned does not prove that every user was satisfied. 两个that分别做什么？|第一个说明fact的内容；第二个引出prove所讨论的内容。|都不是简单把that译成“那个”；many也不能扩大到every。
The centre offers advice to workers whose jobs may disappear. whose修饰什么，may表示什么？|whose jobs指这些工人的工作；may表示可能。|不是已经确认所有岗位都消失；整句说中心向这些工人提供建议。
What the report leaves unclear is how the money will be used. 写两个主要内容单位并翻译。（leave unclear未说明清楚）|What the report leaves unclear是主语；how the money will be used是表语内容。报告没有说清的是这笔钱将如何使用。|不能把what当独立疑问句倒装；money是被使用的对象。
The scientist said that the method which her team developed could be used at home. method是谁开发，在哪里使用？|她的团队开发；可在家使用。|which ... developed修饰method；could be used是that内容中的被动，不能把said当使用动作。
The teachers discussed whether the tests measured skills that mattered outside school. 先后说明whether和that的作用。（measure衡量；matter重要）|whether引出讨论的是否内容；that修饰skills。|讨论的是测试是否衡量校外重要技能，而不是已经确认它们做到了。
The museum, which had been closed for repairs, reopened on Friday. 补充信息是什么？主事件是什么？|此前因维修关闭；周五重新开放。|which从句补充museum的经历；had been closed与reopened有过去先后关系。
The equipment in the rooms near the stairs needs regular checks. needs跟哪个词一致？（equipment设备；stairs楼梯）|equipment。|rooms和stairs位于修饰组内，不能按最近的复数名词决定needs。
Volunteers offered maps to visitors. The latter were unfamiliar with the city. latter指谁？（latter后者）|visitors。|前面依次出现志愿者与游客，后者是游客；语义也支持他们不熟悉城市。
The town reduced bus fares. This helped older residents travel more often. This概括什么？|降低公交票价这一做法／事实。|不能只指复数fares；它连接前一个事件与后面的效果。
Some students read the report, while others listened to a summary. others指哪些人？（summary摘要）|其他学生。|others承接同一讨论群体，并非其他报告；while在这里对比两种做法。
The programme was designed for parents who could not attend daytime classes. 不可忽略哪一项限制？|这些父母不能参加日间课程。|who从句限定目标人群；只译“面向所有父母”扩大了范围。
I know the reason why the meeting was postponed. why从句说明哪个名词？（postpone推迟）|reason。|主句I know the reason；从句说明会议推迟的原因，不是直接提问语序。
The authors argue that money spent on prevention can reduce later costs. 找spent修饰谁、can reduce的主语是什么。（prevention预防）|spent on prevention修饰money；money ...是can reduce的主语。|作者提出观点，并非spent是独立的主句过去时；can仍是潜在作用。
把“The library bought computers. The computers are used by older learners.”合成一个定语从句句子。|The library bought computers that/which are used by older learners.|关系词指向computers，并在从句中作主语；不能重复加they。
把“我想知道这个计划是否适合住在远处的人”写成英语。提供wonder／plan／suitable for／people／live far away。|I wonder whether/if the plan is suitable for people who live far away.|whether/if引出是否内容，who修饰people，不能把两个主语并排而不交代关系。
翻译：The warning that the manager gave us concerned a problem that few people had noticed.（warning警告；concern涉及）|经理给我们的警告涉及一个很少有人注意到的问题。|第一个that修饰warning，第二个修饰problem；few保留很少而不是无人。
翻译并给it找所指：The course taught students a method they could use at work, and many later recommended it.|课程教给学生一种可在工作中使用的方法，后来许多人推荐这种方法。it最自然承接method，但若更大上下文支持course也可能需进一步核对。|这句存在指代解释空间；不能只凭最近词或答案偏好强作唯一。答出合理解释并指出歧义可得分。
''')

lines(3,'非谓语、被动与相对时间：20项',r'''
The students waiting outside were invited into the room. 分别说明waiting、were invited的作用。|waiting outside修饰students；were invited是主句被动谓语。|学生在等待、学生被邀请；不能把were invited理解成学生邀请别人。
The material collected last month is being checked again. 哪次动作更早？什么正在发生？|收集发生在上个月；材料正在被再次检查。|collected修饰material，is being checked是进行被动谓语，两种时间依据不同。
Having read the instructions, Mei completed the form. 谁读、谁填写、顺序怎样？|都是Mei；先读说明，再填表。|having read表达相对完成；不能让instructions成为填写者。
Seen from the hill, the factory looks smaller than expected. seen是否说明“过去看完”？|不说明；它表示工厂是被看的对象。|主句looks给出当前观察，完整意思是从山上看工厂比预想的小。
The room to be used for the interview is next to the stairs. 找主句谓语并说明to be used。|is；to be used修饰room，表示用于面试的房间。|实际使用时间取决于语境，不是主句另一个过去时。
The museum seems to have attracted more visitors this year. 哪部分与seems构成相对先后？|to have attracted表示吸引游客的情况先于或截至现在的判断。|不把to一概说成未来，也不把seems误读为过去式。
She enjoys being asked for advice. 是否断言她现在正在给建议？|不是；说她喜欢被征求意见。|being asked为被动动名词内容；题目又把被询问误换成正在给出建议。
The road being widened will remain closed this week. 谁被拓宽？何者是主句谓语？（widen拓宽；remain保持）|road被拓宽；will remain。|being widened修饰road，不能理解成道路在拓宽其他东西。
The results announced yesterday surprised the researchers. 谁公布、谁吃惊，句子有没有说明公布者？|研究者感到吃惊；results是被公布的结果，句子没有交代公布者。|不能凭researchers最近就推断他们是公布者。
The scheme allows workers to study without leaving their jobs. 说明to study和leaving各接在哪里。|to study承接allows workers；leaving位于介词without后。|意为不离职即可学习，不能把without leaving译成尚未离职但未来一定离职。
改正想表达“走回家时，我看见车站”：Walking home, the station was seen by me.|Walking home, I saw the station.|本题要让walking的执行者I对应主句主语，避免悬垂修饰；不是说被动在所有语境都错误。
将People saw her enter the building.改为被动句，保留原句以enter原形呈现进入动作的结构，不改成强调进行片段的-ing形式。|She was seen to enter the building.|原句是see＋宾语＋原形；改为这种被动结构时用was seen to enter。She was seen entering the building.也是合乎语法的句子，但它采用-ing呈现观察中的活动，不符合本题明确要求保留的结构。不能把它当作普遍错误。
He was made to wait.能否按同一公式把They let him go变成He was let to go？|不能；表示允许通常说He was allowed to go。|make与let的常见被动搭配不同，不是所有原形宾补统一补to。
I regret to say that the event is canceled. 与I regret canceling the event有何区别？|前句遗憾地告知取消消息；后句后悔自己取消活动。|不能只用to未做、-ing已做来解释两者；交际功能不同。
I remembered to send the letter. 是否必定表示信还没寄？|不是；通常表示当时记得寄，而且寄了。|remembered已在过去语境；不定式不自动指定尚未完成。
a book to read与a bench to sit on，为什么后者有on？|read可直接接book；sit与bench的关系需要on。|介词由具体动词搭配决定，不是所有不定式定语都必须额外加介词。
Reading and taking notes are useful. 为什么这里不是is？|两个不同活动并列作主语，通常用复数are。|单个动名词短语配单数的规则不能不看并列结构就套用。
The speaker offered a convincing explanation. convincing能否因为speaker是人就改成convinced？|不能这样改；convincing修饰explanation，意为有说服力的解释。|先找真正修饰对象，再判断意思；词尾不能按整句出现人或物选。
翻译：To avoid delaying the project, the team agreed to share its data.（delay耽误；agree同意）|为了避免耽误项目，团队同意共享其数据。|to avoid为目的，to share承接agreed；delaying位于avoid后，不能把所有to结构都标成目的。
翻译：The report, written for non-specialists, explains how the device works.（non-specialist非专业人士；device设备）|这份面向非专业人士撰写的报告解释了设备的工作方式。|written ...补充说明report；how内容承接explains，不是问句倒装。
''')

lines(4,'范围与逻辑：20项',r'''
原文Some participants improved，选项All participants improved，能否据原文支持？|不能；some不足以支持all。|不代表all永远错误，而是这条证据没有给全体结果。
“Not every attempt succeeded”与“No attempt succeeded”是否同义？|不同；前者并非每次成功，后者没有一次成功。|否定范围不同，不能把部分否定强化为全否定。
The method was less effective than expected. 是否表示完全无效？|不是；效果低于预期不等于无效果。|比较以预期为参照，没有给零效果结论。
The number fell from 100 to 80. fell by多少，fell to多少？|fell by 20；fell to 80。|变化量与最终值不同；若换百分比，则下降20%。
The share rose from 20% to 30%. 是上升10个百分点，还是相对增长10%？|上升10个百分点；相对原20%增长50%。|百分比水平之差与相对变化率不同，原文没说时不要混写。
A is cheaper than B, and B is faster than C. 能推出A比C快吗？|不能。|前一比较涉及价格，后一比较涉及速度，而且没有A与C的速度关系。
People using the service reported lower stress. 能断定服务是唯一原因吗？|不能。|这里只给群体报告的关联，没有排除其他因素。
The policy could reduce traffic.与The policy has reduced traffic同义吗？|不同；前者可能减少，后者已减少。|情态可能与已发生结果不能互换。
The shop closed after the road works began. 是否已证明因修路而关门？|未证明。|after只给时间先后，原因需要其他证据。
Although the tickets were cheap, few people came. 哪个结果成立？|来的人很少，尽管票便宜。|不能把although改成because并保持意思；few不等于没有人。
Unless you book early, a seat cannot be guaranteed. 改写为if结构。（guarantee保证）|If you do not book early, a seat cannot be guaranteed.|本例unless表达例外条件；不能无故再加一个not。
Whether the test is easy or difficult, you should read the instructions. whether表示什么？|无论容易还是困难，都应读说明。|它没有要求先判断是否容易，主句在两种情况下都成立。
Not only students but also teachers use the service. 能否理解成只有学生使用？|不能；学生和老师都使用。|not only ... but also关联两个群体，不是只否定学生。
The article lists price, safety and convenience but does not mention speed. NOT mentioned题应选哪类信息？|speed，速度。|题目找未提到的信息；不能反选确实被列出的安全。
作者说The trial is promising, though more evidence is needed. 能否选“已经充分证实”？|不能；有前景但仍需更多证据。|promising不等于proven；让步后保留不确定性。
原文Most courses are online，选项Some courses are online，是否可以支持？|可以；most通常包含至少有一部分。|范围较弱的陈述可被较强的数量信息支持，不是选项与原词不同就错。
The service is available only to members. 能否推出所有成员都实际用了它？|不能。|资格或可用性不等于实际使用行为。
The plan reduced waiting time but increased costs. 写一个不丢两方面的中文概括。|方案缩短了等待时间，但增加了成本。|不能只保留好处再推成整体毫无代价。
改正不被原文支持的概括：原文“can help some adults”，概括“must help every child”。|可概括为“可能帮助部分成年人”。|须同时修正情态、数量和对象，不是只改一个词。
用英文表达“尽管方法有用，它并不适合所有人”。提供although／useful／suitable for／everyone。|Although the method is useful, it is not suitable for everyone.|保留让步与部分适用限制；不能译为nobody can use it。
''')

block(5,'单空对话：五项','选出同时符合前后语境的回应。',[
mc('A: Would you mind moving your bag? B: ____ I will put it under my seat.', ['Not at all.','Thank you for the bag.','I am afraid you are late.','It costs ten pounds.'],'Not at all.','后句承诺移包，表示不介意；感谢、迟到、价格均不承接请求。'),
mc('A: I am sorry I sent the wrong file. B: ____ Please send the correct one now.', ['These things happen.','Congratulations on your success.','I prefer tea.','The office closes yesterday.'],'These things happen.','接受道歉后提出补救；祝贺、饮品无关；The office closes yesterday把一般现在时closes与已结束的yesterday相配，时间形式也不合适。'),
mc('A: Could we meet on Tuesday instead? B: ____ I have a meeting all day.', ['I am afraid Tuesday will not work.','Tuesday would be perfect.','Thanks for explaining the route.','I have already read the book.'],'I am afraid Tuesday will not work.','all day meeting解释不能赴约；perfect与后文冲突，其余话题无关。'),
mc('A: Thank you for showing me the way. B: ____',['You are welcome.','I cannot agree to cancel it.','That is a difficult spelling.','No, it was expensive.'],'You are welcome.','回应感谢；其他选项分别引入取消、拼写、价格，缺少上下文依据。'),
mc('A: How long does the application take? B: ____ A: Then I should apply this week.', ['About ten working days.','At the main office.','Because it is popular.','A blue cover.'],'About ten working days.','how long问时长，后句据此计划；地点、原因和物品特征都答非所问。'),
])
block(5,'整段对话一：预约','选项各使用一次。\n\nA. Would Friday morning be possible?\nB. What time would suit you?\nC. I will send you a confirmation.\n\nPatient: I need to change my appointment.\nReceptionist: Of course. What day do you prefer?\nPatient: 【1】\nReceptionist: Yes. 【2】\nPatient: Ten o\'clock, please.\nReceptionist: Fine. 【3】',[
op('空1选哪一句？','A','前面问日期，回答星期五上午；B问具体时间，C表示确认，应在后面。'),
op('空2选哪一句？','B','下一句Ten o’clock给时间，需询问具体时间；不是另约日期或结束确认。'),
op('空3选哪一句？','C','日期与时间确认后发送确认，完成预约过程；另两项已完成对应功能。'),
])
block(5,'整段对话二：共同学习','选项各使用一次。\n\nA. What do you find most difficult?\nB. Let us practise explaining them to each other.\nC. I can bring my notes.\n\nLin: I am having trouble with the course.\nSam: 【1】\nLin: I understand the examples, but I cannot explain the rules.\nSam: 【2】\nLin: Good idea. Shall we meet after class?\nSam: Yes. 【3】',[
op('空1选哪一句？','A','后句解释具体困难，空白处应追问困难。'),op('空2选哪一句？','B','them承接rules，建议互相解释；Good idea作接受回应。'),op('空3选哪一句？','C','承接课后复习安排，带笔记是具体准备；不再重复追问已明确的困难。'),
])
block(5,'整段对话三：访谈','选项各使用一次。\n\nA. What first interested you in this work?\nB. Did you receive any training?\nC. How do you deal with disagreement?\nD. What do you hope to do next?\n\nInterviewer: 【1】\nVolunteer: I wanted to help older neighbours use online services.\nInterviewer: 【2】\nVolunteer: Yes. The library taught us how to explain each step clearly.\nInterviewer: 【3】\nVolunteer: I listen first and ask people to describe their problem.\nInterviewer: 【4】\nVolunteer: I would like to train more volunteers.',[
op('空1选哪一句？','A','回答说明最初动机；不是培训经历。'),op('空2选哪一句？','B','Yes和taught us对应是否受训。'),op('空3选哪一句？','C','回答描述处理分歧的方式，不是未来打算。'),op('空4选哪一句？','D','would like和train more volunteers回答未来希望。'),
])

vocab = [
('Only eligible applicants may join the programme. 选择eligible在本句的近义词。',['qualified','available','careless','wealthy'],'qualified','eligible说符合申请资格；available有空或可用，careless粗心，wealthy富有，都不是资格条件。'),
('The team will assess the environmental impact. 替换assess。',['evaluate','ignore','produce','delay'],'evaluate','评估影响，而不是忽略、产生或推迟影响。'),
('Periodic inspections are required. 替换Periodic。',['Regular','Constant','Accidental','Final'],'Regular','定期与regular对应；constant是不间断，accidental偶然，final最终。'),
('The old documents are fragile. 替换fragile。',['delicate','valuable','modern','lengthy'],'delicate','容易损坏接近delicate；不自动等于有价值、现代或很长。'),
('The proposal is feasible with the current budget. 替换feasible。',['practical','permanent','famous','compulsory'],'practical','现有预算下可行；永久、著名、强制均改变判断方向。'),
('The report revealed a serious weakness. 替换revealed。',['disclosed','concealed','created','repaired'],'disclosed','揭示已有弱点；conceal隐藏，create制造，repair修复。'),
('Residents were reluctant to accept the change. 替换reluctant。',['unwilling','unable','forbidden','delighted'],'unwilling','不情愿是意愿，不等于无能力、被禁止或高兴。'),
('The course helps learners acquire practical skills. 替换acquire。',['obtain','require','forget','donate'],'obtain','获得技能；require是需要或要求，形近不能替换。'),
('The organisation aims to retain experienced staff. 替换retain。',['keep','replace','dismiss','retrain'],'keep','保留员工；replace替换，dismiss解雇，retrain重新培训。'),
('The benefit gradually diminished. 替换diminished。',['decreased','vanished immediately','remained unchanged','became certain'],'decreased','逐渐减少不等于立即消失；其余是保持或确定性，均不对应。'),
('The team maintained the service during the repairs. 替换maintained。',['sustained','suspended','abandoned','advertised'],'sustained','维修时维持服务；suspend暂停，abandon放弃，advertise宣传。'),
('The new design is appealing to young users. 替换appealing。',['attractive','frightening','compulsory','familiar'],'attractive','有吸引力；不能与形近的appalling混同，其他词不表达吸引。'),
('The available evidence is adequate for this decision. 替换adequate。',['sufficient','excessive','irrelevant','unreliable'],'sufficient','对决定足够；过量、无关和不可靠均是不同判断。'),
('Prior experience is not required. 替换Prior。',['Previous','Future','Shared','Unusual'],'Previous','先前经验；不是未来、共同或特殊经验。'),
('The delay was due to a shortage of staff. due to最接近哪项？',['caused by','followed by','despite','in addition to'],'caused by','表原因；followed by只是先后，despite让步，in addition to递进。'),
('The system is intended to reduce waste. intended to接近哪项？',['designed to','proven to','unable to','required not to'],'designed to','目的或设计意图，不保证已证明有效；不能变成无能力或禁止。'),
('The policy had a substantial effect, though problems remained. 替换substantial。',['considerable','minor','accidental','temporary'],'considerable','效果可观但不保证完全解决；小、偶然和临时分别改变程度、方式、时间。'),
('The campaign seeks to raise awareness. 本句raise接近哪项？',['increase','rise','borrow','conceal'],'increase','及物raise提高意识；rise通常不及物，不能直接接awareness，borrow和conceal意义不合。'),
('Higher demand resulted in longer waiting times. 改写resulted in。',['led to','came from','prevented','was identical to'],'led to','需求高导致等待长；came from会反转原因结果，prevented相反，identical不是因果。'),
('The editor called for a thorough review. 替换thorough。',['comprehensive','rapid','occasional','superficial'],'comprehensive','全面彻底；快速或偶尔不是同一维度，superficial表面肤浅是反方向。'),
]
block(6,'语境替换：20题','目标词已经在每题指明。先判断它在本句的意思，再把候选真正代回。', [mc(*row) for row in vocab])
block(6,'词汇填空备用形式：10题','大纲也允许词汇部分采用选词填空。以下空白要同时满足结构、搭配与上下文意义。',[
mc('The launch had to wait because the final safety checks were not yet ____.',['completed','optional','public','similar'],'completed','检查尚未完成是继续等待的原因；是否可选、公开或相似不表达完成状态。'),
mc('The service accepts every resident, ____ age or income.',['regardless of','because of','instead of','apart from'],'regardless of','every resident与不分年龄收入一致；因为、代替、排除都会改变范围。'),
mc('The report shows an association, but it does not ____ that one change caused the other.',['prove','prefer','borrow','purchase'],'prove','相关不等于证明因果；偏好、借用、购买都不适合that因果内容。'),
mc('The centre needs a ____ supply of trained staff, not occasional help.',['steady','brief','rare','reluctant'],'steady','not occasional形成持续稳定与偶尔的对比；短暂、稀少、不情愿不合供给要求。'),
mc('Learners requested an evening session. The centre added one ____ their feedback.',['in response to','in place of','in contrast to','in spite of'],'in response to','新增晚课回应同一请求；不是取代反馈、与反馈相反或不顾反馈。'),
mc('Visitors may use the equipment only after registration; registration is therefore a ____ for access.',['requirement','consequence','reward','prediction'],'requirement','only after给进入条件，故是要求；不是进入后的结果、奖励或预测。'),
mc('The two surveys used different methods, so their figures cannot be ____ directly.',['compared','forgotten','advertised','owned'],'compared','方法不同限制直接比较；忘记、宣传、拥有不表达数据可比性。'),
mc('A clear label may ____ confusion by showing users where to begin.',['reduce','create','conceal','justify'],'reduce','明确起点是减少困惑的机制；创造、掩藏、为困惑辩解不合解释。'),
mc('The timetable is a proposal rather than a final decision; it remains open to ____.',['revision','punishment','payment','ownership'],'revision','proposal与非最终状态允许修改；惩罚、付款、所有权都不对应对未定方案作修改。'),
mc('The scheme can work ____ there are enough trained volunteers; without them it must stop.',['provided that','although','as though','in order that'],'provided that','后半without ... stop明确条件；不是虽然、仿佛或为了某目的。'),
])
